BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artist Talk with Will Kasso Condry of Juniper Creative Arts
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260903
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTSTAMP:20260902T150909Z
UID:40bfeb32951b9cfb6517ddc458bc4b@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Meet artist and co-founder of Juniper Creative Arts\, Will Kas
 so Condry\, for a tour of his solo exhibition Everything is Everything\, f
 ollowed by a group discussion. Exploring the intersection of community and
  the positive impact of art\, Kasso Condry discusses his creative practice
 \, journey of healing\, and family mythology. BCA’s Summer exhibitions a
 re supported in part by the Maslow Family Foundation. Hospitality sponsors
 \, Sugarsnap and Lake Champlain Chocolates. Burlington City Arts is suppor
 ted in part by the Vermont Arts Council & the National Endowment for the A
 rts.\n\nSources: Vermont.com\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Burlington City Arts\, Burlington\, VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/artist-tal
 k-with-will-kasso-condry-of-juniper-creative-arts-21-08-2026-13-46-13
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:August Exhibitions + Opening Reception at Bryan Gallery in Jeffers
 onville
DTSTART:20260903T170000
DTEND:20260903T190000
DTSTAMP:20260902T150909Z
UID:87e14cc1b87e1ac8aa40bba9084357@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Land & Light & Water & Air [August 26 – October 25] Main Gal
 lery The Gallery’s largest exhibit of traditional landscape and plein ai
 r works\, this is also the Gallery's flagship exhibit. The exhibit contain
 s a blend of works by artists who frequently show in the Gallery\, as well
  as some of our newest artists. The 100+ works in this exhibit visually br
 ing viewers to beautiful vistas around New England\, in mediums that range
  from painted silks to watercolor and gouache. This is the only exhibit fo
 r which the Gallery presents awards. Postcards from Here [August 26 – Oc
 tober 25] Middle Room Gallery This exhibit re-imagines vintage postcards\,
  capturing the nostalgia of travel to special places\, and remembering the
 m with keepsake cards. As mailed letters and cards continue to decline\, t
 his display celebrates a time when hand-addressed mail was special and hig
 hly anticipated. Opening Reception & Award Ceremony: Thursday\, September 
 3\, 5 – 7pm\, in Jeffersonville Celebrate with us! Meet our artists and 
 snack on homemade treats. Enjoy remarks from our Gallery Director and awar
 d presentations. Free and open to the public!\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Bryan Art Gallery\, 180 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/august-exh
 ibitions-opening-reception-at-bryan-gallery-in-jeffersonville-03-08-2026-1
 1-59-33
END:VEVENT
